## How to read these

- Margin (95%) — the range after a percentage. With this many cases, the true value is very likely inside that range; fewer cases mean a wider range. Below 10 cases we print "—" instead of a percentage, because a rate from so few cases is mostly luck.
- Merged is not the same as correct. A merged PR may still have been a bad change that nobody caught.
- Open PRs are not failures; they count as "not merged" until they merge. Closed-without-merge is not recorded, so it also counts as not merged.
- Evidence records only exist since 2026-10-08, and reverts have only been linked to their PR since 2026-10-15. Older PRs are simply not in the data.
- Backfilled records (created for PRs that merged before recording began) carry no AI verdicts, so they add to coverage but not to the reviewer-confidence numbers.
- Nothing in this report is read by anything that decides whether a PR may merge. It records; it does not gate.

## What is not reported yet and why

- CI gate (claim vs verdict) totals — not reported by any hive build yet.
- Median time-to-merge per autonomy level — no selected hive reports it yet (it needs a build that records when each merged PR was opened).
- Revert rate by author kind per hive — not reported by any hive build yet.

## Grade per section

"Not enough data" means the graded rate is below the minimum sample; "Not graded" means there is no good or bad value for that section.

| Section | Grade | How the grade is decided |
|---|---|---|
| Evidence coverage | Fair | Share of merged PRs (90 days) that have an evidence record; Strong at or above 80%, Fair at or above 40%, otherwise Weak. |
| Reviewer confidence | Strong | Share of verdicts that went wrong in the most-confident range with enough verdicts (needs two measurable ranges); Strong at or below 10%, Fair at or below 25%, otherwise Weak. |
| Outcome by author kind | Fair | Revert rate of PRs written by AI agents (humans if no agent PRs); Strong at or below 5%, Fair at or below 15%, otherwise Weak. |
| Autonomy level × outcome | Fair | Revert rate at the highest autonomy level with enough merged PRs; Strong at or below 5%, Fair at or below 15%, otherwise Weak. |
| Boundary enforcement | Not graded | There is no "good" block rate: zero blocks with many attempts means agents stayed inside their lane, many blocks means the guardrail did its job. |
| Same- vs cross-family review | Fair | False-approve rate of the family mix with the most verdicts; Strong at or below 10%, Fair at or below 25%, otherwise Weak. |
| Per-hive evidence | Fair | Share of selected hives reporting for the window (no minimum sample); Strong at or above 80%, Fair at or above 40%, otherwise Weak. |
| Shadow gates | Weak | False-alarm rate (PRs a gate would have held that merged and stuck) of the gate with the most held PRs; Strong at or below 25%, Fair at or below 50%, otherwise Weak. |

